# EvoMap Nightly Validation Loop — DRY-RUN cron example
# =============================================================================
# ATL-EVOMAP-8A ships this file ONLY as an example / template.
#
# This file MUST NOT be installed by this phase.
# Installing real cron / systemd timers is a separate, operator-owned action
# (a future ATL-EVOMAP-8B phase or manual operator step), gated on:
#
#   * the runner smoke test passing at least once (this phase)
#   * explicit human authorization to install real cron
#   * the runner + manifest being audited
#
# To install manually later, an operator would copy the snippet below into
# /etc/cron.d/evomap-nightly (or the operator's own preferred scheduler)
# AFTER replacing /path/to/ai-tool-test-lab with the real path on the
# operator's machine.
# =============================================================================

# Recommended cadence: daily 02:30 Asia/Shanghai
# (after the 02:00 wiki compiler if present, before any operator session)
SHELL=/bin/bash
PATH=/usr/local/sbin:/usr/local/bin:/usr/sbin:/usr/bin:/sbin:/bin
TZ=Asia/Shanghai

# Nightly EvoMap validation loop
# -- writes digest JSON + Markdown + run log under the case phase artifacts/
# -- exits 0 on clean PASS, 1 on any blocking FAIL
30 2 * * * cd /path/to/ai-tool-test-lab && /usr/bin/python3 scripts/evomap_nightly_validate.py --output-dir cases/evomap-evolver-openclaw-v0/phase8a-nightly-validation-loop/artifacts >> /var/log/evomap-nightly.log 2>&1
